# Wave W17-X (Route 210): ranch turf — ranch meadow, deep grass flecks: the deepest green in the tranche, a saturated pasture carrying straw and hay-gold flecks, the grass the sign promises deepens north toward the towers (design: fenced paddocks and deepening grass; the EMBERFOAL herd bunched at the north fence — the herd is creature layer, the deep grass is this ground). Route 210’s own ground — split from Route 209’s muted pilgrim sage by depth and appetite entire, and from its own North segment’s fog murk by clarity: this is the clear road, the fog is still coming.
